{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/141362-trying-to-come-up-with-a-basis-for-a-skin-thief-compact-conspericy","id":141362,"title":"Trying to come up with a basis for a skin-thief compact/conspericy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-18T01:35:21-07:00","id":141362,"title":"Trying to come up with a basis for a skin-thief compact/conspericy","content":"The endowments are simple enough (follows the same guidelines as World of Darkness: Skinchangers book) but I have trouble trying to nail stuff down. Any ideas that could help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T01:46:40-07:00","id":141384,"title":"","content":"What are you needing help nailing down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T01:55:41-07:00","id":141410,"title":"","content":"Mostly the overall structure of the organization. As it currently stands, the organization much akin to a tier three organization in term (given the simple facts that it has endowments) but I keep hitting mental roadblocks when it comes to building the organization's core ethos. I could make them akin hating the Uratha as the AKD does (Wolf-blooded simply having enough of their relatives shit is a thought) or I could cast their net wider beyond just the Uratha. If worse comes to worse, I could simply drop the Changing Breeds in there to give them focus but putting that in there leaves a bad taste in my mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T10:29:43-07:00","id":141683,"title":"","content":"Well, let's look at one of the more common ideas involving skin-thieving in RL folklore: the wearing of an animal's pelt to attain or steal its power(s). Thus, the core ethos could follow that structure, in that everything has power and a name, and attaining one or the other grants you a measure of control or power over that thing. Gain both, and you are free to use the guise and identity of that other thing as you please. They are like a reverse version of the W:tF hosts \u2014 instead of gaining a fleshy shell to multiply, survive and wreak havoc on the world because it is their nature, they gain fleshy, sometimes even ethereal forms to control, keep order and, if need be, give their lives for whatever purpose you have in mind.<br /> <br /> This doesn't put them above using the guises of other humans for their needs. Think of the Faceless Men from <i>Game of Thrones</i> if you need a comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T11:04:34-07:00","id":141716,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'd take inspiration from the comic Crimson and the Red Hood's Revenge: the Red Hoods, signified by their reversable red hoods, red hoods while hunting, but wolf pelt on the inside, when reversed they take the wolf's power for their own.<br /> <br /> Once there was a young girl in a red hood, and the big bad wolf ate her grandmother, fed the girl granny's flesh, and took her in her grandmother's bed. They say he consumed her, but when it was over, his skinless corpse was thrown in the river weighted with rocks, and she left with a new skin on her shoulders and a child in her belly. <br /> <br /> The core of the red hoods is said to be that girl's descendants, but who can say, after all this time? They recruit from those victimized by werewolves and other feral monsters, give people the chance to take their destinies back, claim the powers of a monster for their own, <br /> <br /> When their hoods are red, they hunt using hexcraft, the secrets of the spirits, begged, borrowed, and stolen, but wolfhooded they bay at the moon and hunt as a pack. <br /> <br /> Are you a legacy? Taught how to hunt since you were old enough to walk, taught hexes at your grandmother's knee? Are you a wolfblood, paying back your own family's betrayal with magic and silver? Were you a victim? You're family devoured for essence or blood while the horror broke your mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T06:52:19-07:00","id":143379,"title":"","content":"Don't worry too much about making them Tier 3 just because they have an Endowment. If they work better as Tier 2, go for it.<br /> <br /> Now my suggestions would be that skin-stealing doesn't quite lend itself to a cause; so you'll have to think of a mission that skin-stealing can be useful for. Maybe they consider themselves the last remains of some long lost culture, and they want to find the sleeping Spirit of their culture and wake it up. Hence skin-stealing to get into the Spirit world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T12:01:54-07:00","id":143767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/141362-trying-to-come-up-with-a-basis-for-a-skin-thief-compact-conspericy?p=143379#post143379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry too much about making them Tier 3 just because they have an Endowment. If they work better as Tier 2, go for it.<br /> <br /> Now my suggestions would be that skin-stealing doesn't quite lend itself to a cause; so you'll have to think of a mission that skin-stealing can be useful for. Maybe they consider themselves the last remains of some long lost culture, and they want to find the sleeping Spirit of their culture and wake it up. Hence skin-stealing to get into the Spirit world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now, I'm mostly picturing a bunch of independent cells discovering a series of different skin-thief rituals and it's only recently (the last 200 years) that they've started to come together and compare notes as it where. That type of structure leads more to Compact than anything else.<br /> <br /> The endowments are equally going to tricky as Skinthevies are incredibly diverse lot. Different rituals for acquiring the form of same animal. The same ritual for acquiring the form of different animals, and complete smattering of results in every direction.<br /> <br /> I may have to break the endowments up in the same path that Knights of St George has them. One faction is geared towards being bloody bastards (Their newly sharpened predatory instincts demand to hunt something. Uratha, Mortals, even other Hunters are all on the list) and focuses being able to change into predatory shapes (Bears, Wolves, Eagles, etc),<br /> <br /> Another is dedicated to peeking into the Shadow and dealing with spirits, while the last is weird...<br /> <br /> For the last one, I'm toying with the idea of making it hive orientated. In the natural world, there is social order in crows, herd animals, and insects so their endowments would be up to the gills in being able to command minions and bringing to bare collective power upon enemies that piss them off. Much akin to what a Mummy Cult has but much more low powered.<br /> <br /> The theme I might want to go with is the overall feel of constant bickering within the Compact. There are real ideological differences that are constantly expressed and the animal instincts in a lot of the members only amplify this trait. It may very well be that the lower status people that carry the weight of carrying the structure of the compact as the elders are much more inclined to rip each other apart rather than talk like human beings.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T12:18:14-07:00","id":148851,"title":"","content":"Is going to be any difference between their spirit pacts and <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Les Myst\u00e8res\u00b4 rites du cheval?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T14:04:58-07:00","id":148926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/141362-trying-to-come-up-with-a-basis-for-a-skin-thief-compact-conspericy?p=148851#post148851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is going to be any difference between their spirit pacts and <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Les Myst\u00e8res\u00b4 rites du cheval?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Les Mysteries are shamans who call and make pacts with spirits. While the relationship can be confrontational, it's usually cooperative between the two. The Skinthief compact that I have in mind is much more adversarial and antagonistic toward spirits in general. <br /> <br /> Think of them going into the Shadow on hunting expeditions, working to bring down a spirit (or spirits), then consuming it's essence via their rituals and thus being able to mimic the spirit's abilities and skin for a brief amount of time much like the Prometheus Brotherhood does with Mages.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons why I like this idea because it makes the Uratha collectively shit bricks. They take humans for granted when it comes the spirit realm and now you suddenly have the revelation of humans coming into the Shadow, beating the crap out of spirits, consuming their power and taking their skins, and being able to pose as that spirit as some kind of sleeper agent for the purpose of adding to more hunts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T19:12:25-07:00","id":149067,"title":"","content":"What about when one of them goes after a <i>magath</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T21:03:07-07:00","id":149122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/141362-trying-to-come-up-with-a-basis-for-a-skin-thief-compact-conspericy?p=149067#post149067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about when one of them goes after a <i>magath</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally treat it like any other spirit and hope they can beat it down and consume before it beats them down or runs off. Magaths for all intents and purposes are spirits who found their way outside their primary purpose (and in my opinion, mutations that can go on to produce their own choirs), and suffer the same rules.<br /> <br /> However, it should be said that these types of Skin thieves tend to start thinking like spirits after a while and will occasionally pick a certain choir to prey on over others as a result. Over time, this can result in certain... problems in terms of how the cell's members relates back the world of the humans. The risk of going native is high and more than one cell has been cannibalized via one of it's members drifting too far into the predatory mindset of spirits. <br /> <br /> Weirder spirits like Abyssal, Infernal, or Idigam would be up to the ST to construct what kind of horror that crap would pop out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T00:19:10-07:00","id":149190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is one of the reasons why I like this idea because it makes the Uratha collectively shit bricks. They take humans for granted when it comes the spirit realm and now you suddenly have the revelation of humans coming into the Shadow, beating the crap out of spirits, consuming their power and taking their skins, and being able to pose as that spirit as some kind of sleeper agent for the purpose of adding to more hunts. </div> </div> </div>Did they punch Cthulhu? :0<br /> No seriously, how muggles can do <b>that</b>? Spirits are damn powerful even for Uratha\u00b4s standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T03:50:08-07:00","id":149294,"title":"","content":"Well the description takes a few liberties with how spirit-skinners are supposed to work.<br /> <br /> Normally a spirit-skinner uses a spirits bans to entrap a spirit, and then use a ritual to either drain its energy or kill it and skin it, to don its form like a cloak, and spirit-skinners have no ability to enter the spirit world unless they don the form of a spirit, in which case they'd be fighting a spirit with another spirit's powers.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that a would be spirit-skinner couldn't enter the hisil through a locus and then mug a spirit of its skin, but that is hardly normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T10:30:34-07:00","id":149499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/141362-trying-to-come-up-with-a-basis-for-a-skin-thief-compact-conspericy?p=149294#post149294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well the description takes a few liberties with how spirit-skinners are supposed to work.<br /> <br /> Normally a spirit-skinner uses a spirits bans to entrap a spirit, and then use a ritual to either drain its energy or kill it and skin it, to don its form like a cloak, and spirit-skinners have no ability to enter the spirit world unless they don the form of a spirit, in which case they'd be fighting a spirit with another spirit's powers.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that a would be spirit-skinner couldn't enter the hisil through a locus and then mug a spirit of its skin, but that is hardly normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct that it's taking a few liberties. I originally thought of them hunting down Hosts or the Claimed but decided to make them more of a pain in the Uratha's side in terms of going into the Shadow and hunting there.<br /> <br /> I may revert to that to making that the default hunting grounds and making opening doors into the Shadow a rank 5 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T17:32:25-07:00","id":151854,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd see them as a Tier 2 organization, similar to Network Zero, and with as much potential of elevation to Tier 3.<br /> <br /> There are three ways I could see the organization:<br /> <br /> <b>The Primals: </b>These are the Skin-Theives who claim the power of spirits to gain the might and cunning of a primeval era, a time when outside the settlement was full of predators for the hairless apes. Primals take on the form and might of spirits as a way to even the battlefield between Man and the things that go bump in the night, as a way to feel the strength of the storm and the swiftness of cheetah, and as a way to enforce their will on the neighboring human tribes. These are the ones whose teachings center on upholding both the Vigil and the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> In modern day there are a few Primals left, though even one with the combined might of Elephant, Rhinoceros, and Gorilla would be cut down by a handful of 6 year olds with AK-47s. The traditions passed down from father to son and mentor to student leave them prepared for when technology fails and the last electric lightbulb dims, and the predators return.<br /> <br /> AKA: Regressives, Beast-men, Goons, Jungle Watchmen, Children of Gaia<br /> Concepts: Ultra-survivalists, tribal protectors, stalkers of the night<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Givers: </b>These Skin-Theives study, absorb, and observe spirits to gain an awareness of an object or environment only appreciable to those who have existed as that object or environment. &quot;To become a thing is to know a thing, and to assume its form is to begin to understand its existence&quot; is a favored aphorism of theirs, and guides their philosophy on shapeshifting. With each spirit consumed and their existence studied from the inside, they feel they honor the spirit by fulfilling its nature while taking its form.<br /> <br /> Givers in the modern day seek to understand the evolving interaction between Man and Nature, now that Man has imposed such change upon Nature. Their traditions teach of ministering both to spirits and Man, to guide the two into a symbiotic relationship. Teaching Man of their place as an equal member of Nature as opposed to master of it, and teaching Spirits patience at the complex, strange, and aggressive species that so often is blind to them.<br /> <br /> AKA: Watchers, Receivers of Wisdom, Students of Gaia<br /> Concepts: Zoologists, Scientists, Shaman<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Neolutionists:</b> These Skin-Theives show that the only constant is change. While their name is strictly modern-day, the philosophy of the Neolutionists is the original, from the very first time the hominid brain could begin to think: that of seizing their own destiny. These Skin-Theives hunt and consume spirits to change towards their own personal ideal of perfection. Most Neolutionists tend towards places of creation and change, hoping to integrate the fluctuating natures of like spirits into their own. Some enterprising Neolutionists bargain with more powerful examples of these spirits for use of their Numen instead of trying to reverse-engineer the abilities.<br /> <br /> Each Neolutionist has their own ideal they seek to attain, but almost all agree it involves more than the body they were born with is capable of. Some of the more experienced Neolutionists can seem like something out of the mind of Lovecraft or Giger, though these are thankfully few, far between, and tend to disappear before long. If they disappear into the Shadow, are killed off by Hunters, are descended upon by other Neolutionists, or ascend to another plane of existence, nobody can say for sure. The actual effect of a Neolutionist's 'activities' on their genetic descendents is similarly up for debate, though certainly more than a few have guided their own development with an eye for passing on traits.<br /> <br /> AKA: Freaks, Progressives, Loonies, The Clear-Eyed, Chrysali,<br /> Concepts: Body-modifier, bleeding-edge technologist, Renaissance Man","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T19:23:20-07:00","id":153373,"title":"","content":"Comments? Critiques? I admit I may have gotten a random thought inspired by the name &quot;Skin-Theives&quot; and completely missed if everyone else was basing their discussion on something actually published.......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T21:14:59-07:00","id":153466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/141362-trying-to-come-up-with-a-basis-for-a-skin-thief-compact-conspericy?p=153373#post153373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comments? Critiques? I admit I may have gotten a random thought inspired by the name &quot;Skin-Theives&quot; and completely missed if everyone else was basing their discussion on something actually published.......</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, been a bit busy with a few projects of mine. Should have my thoughts on the matter tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}